      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to consider the number of games each pair of teams plays and then sum these for all pairs.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of unique pairs of teams. Since there are 9 teams, the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{9}{2} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique pairs of teams.\n\nNext, each pair of teams plays exactly 3 games. Therefore, the total number of games played is the number of unique pairs multiplied by the number of games each pair plays:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 3 = 108\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played in the season is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
